-- Update only the unedited kitchen starting brief; preserve personal edits.
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Treat A+B+C as one year-round kitchen, dining and living volume. A is the long west extension, B the shallow north return, C the existing kitchen, and D the existing east cooker wall. Use the confirmed source-plan outline and proportions in every option; do not rotate, mirror, deepen B or enlarge the envelope. Compare three layouts: a larger social kitchen in C with dining in A and lounging in B; a relocated working kitchen in A with dining in C and breakfast in B; and a family lounge in A with dining at the northwest corner and a redesigned kitchen in C. The island and cooker may move where the selected plan explicitly proposes it. Wider north and west openings are proposals, with retained piers shown as assumptions pending structural review. Follow each selected plan and deterministic cutaway model before using its AI illustration as a finish reference. Use warm timber, limestone, slim glazing and the natural character of the house. Furniture fit, ceiling height, supports and service routes are not verified. Actual approved drawings and measured dimensions remain outstanding.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='kitchen' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Start from the confirmed A+B footprint traced on the original exposé inset: A is the long WEST wing alongside the existing kitchen; B is the shallower NORTH return; C is the existing kitchen; D is its EAST cooker wall. The owner confirmed this outline on 14 September 2026. Keep these proportions and orientation in every study. The approximately 40 m² reported in the exposé is not a measured area verification. Explore a year-round kitchen and dining room with expanded preparation and storage, generous glazing, timber and stone. Begin by comparing a freestanding west-wing dining table with a west-side banquette; the north return can be a sitting or reading edge. Keep the existing cooker wall and island as starting anchors. Test improvements to the existing kitchen working area. Do not assume large wall removals or a deep north dining room. Preserve source openings in initial layouts; any enlarged opening is a separate structural proposal. Verify furniture clearances, dimensions, roof and approved drawings before producing geometry-based interior views. The earlier kitchen images and their inferred layouts have been discarded.';
